import{_ as i,o as t,c as n,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 429 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Causal Self-Discipline Absence: Transmigrators and Causal Disturbance","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 429 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Causal Self-Discipline Absence: Transmigrators and Causal Disturbance","no":429,"module":2,"tags":["Manghuang Ji","Causal Self-Discipline","Transmigrator","Causal Disturbance","Cross-Plane"],"related":["83-Observe-First-Then-Limited-Interference Principle","87-Knowledge-Return-Only Principle","89-Time-Paradox Prevention Mechanism"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0429_模块2-莽荒纪-因果自律缺失-穿越者与因果扰动.md","filePath":"en/0429_模块2-莽荒纪-因果自律缺失-穿越者与因果扰动.md"}'),s={name:"en/0429_模块2-莽荒纪-因果自律缺失-穿越者与因果扰动.md"};function o(r,e,l,c,d,u){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="entry-429-manghuang-system-decomposition-·-causal-self-discipline-absence-transmigrators-and-causal-disturbance" tabindex="-1">Entry 429 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Causal Self-Discipline Absence: Transmigrators and Causal Disturbance <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-429-manghuang-system-decomposition-·-causal-self-discipline-absence-transmigrators-and-causal-disturbance" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 429 | Manghuang System Decomposition · Causal Self-Discipline Absence: Transmigrators and Causal Disturbance&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Manghuang Ji Full Decomposition (Entry 34) | Benchmark base: Documents 83, 87, 89</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-an-airdropped-foreign-soul-on-what-grounds-does-it-not-settle-accounts-with-causality" tabindex="-1">Introduction: an airdropped foreign soul, on what grounds does it not settle accounts with causality <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-an-airdropped-foreign-soul-on-what-grounds-does-it-not-settle-accounts-with-causality" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: an airdropped foreign soul, on what grounds does it not settle accounts with causality&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the <strong>causal self-discipline axiom</strong> is this entry&#39;s core — cross-plane operations strictly filed; observe first then limited interference; return only knowledge, do not disturb causality. Ji Ning is a transmigrator: a modern soul airdropped into Manghuang&#39;s world, enjoying the time-difference dividend, yet never filing, never settling. This entry specifically discusses this causal self-discipline absence. The law-first axiom is core. Protagonist uniqueness dependency = high-leaning-medium. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s judging base has been upgraded to the six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A transmigrator&#39;s causal waste lies in &quot;disturbance without correction&quot;: Ji Ning airdrops with past-life cognition, changes Manghuang world&#39;s evolution curve, yet no mechanism corrects the disturbance back. <strong>A foreign variable injected into a native system, yet the system has no feedback loop — this is energy waste at the causal level.</strong></p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>How causal disturbance manufactures regression:</p><ol><li><strong>Evolution tugged off course</strong>: native civilization tugged by transmigrator&#39;s past-life experience in a specific direction, losing native diversity</li><li><strong>Karmic debt accumulates</strong>: every disturbance accumulates unsettled debt</li><li><strong>Time-paradox risk</strong>: the further the transmigrator changes, the more complex the paradox; late propped up by &quot;plot rounding&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Behind causal absence is the transmigrator defaulting on the &quot;cross-plane bill&quot;:</p><ul><li><strong>Time-difference dividend free-taken</strong>: past-life cognition is pure increment, yet pays no price</li><li><strong>No filing, no observation</strong>: no &quot;observe first&quot; procedure before airdropping</li><li><strong>Take without settle</strong>: takes cultivation adventures from Manghuang world, yet does not settle with native causality</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Manghuang Causal Absence</th><th>Anchor-Symbiosis Causal Institutions</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Transmigrator freely airdrops</td><td>Cross-plane operations strictly filed</td></tr><tr><td>Change first, observe later</td><td>Observe-first-then-limited-interference principle</td></tr><tr><td>Free-take time-difference dividend</td><td>Knowledge-return-only principle: transmit knowledge only, do not disturb</td></tr><tr><td>Karmic debt accumulates</td><td>Time-paradox prevention mechanism: external variables monitored throughout</td></tr><tr><td>Disturbance uncorrected</td><td>Archaeology protocol: low-pollution intervention; preserve native evolution</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate &quot;no-filing transmigration,&quot; &quot;filing + knowledge-return-only,&quot; &quot;complete isolation&quot; three cross-plane intervention modes</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: observe native civilization&#39;s off-course degree, karmic-debt accumulation</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: native-evolution curve deviation, native-original rate, time-paradox risk</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: quantified conclusion — under no-filing model native evolution significantly tugged off course; under filing + knowledge-return-only model native evolution protected</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Manghuang causal setting self-consistency: low</strong>. The conflict between transmigrator&#39;s past-life memory and native causality never deeply inquired</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: medium-high</strong>. Causal line rounded by plot; early &quot;fate,&quot; late &quot;change fate&quot;</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: high-leaning-medium</strong>. The transmigrator halo is Ji Ning&#39;s hidden pillar of success</li></ul><p>Causal self-discipline absence also has an often-overlooked angle: it lets the transmigrator forever live in moral immunity. Whatever Ji Ning does he need not be responsible, because he is an outsider; Manghuang&#39;s causality cannot reach him. Once this immunity holds, the transmigrator has incentive to keep increasing disturbance — anyway no settlement. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s causal supervision precisely breaks this immunity: an external variable is also a variable; once disturbed it must be recorded, evaluated, corrected. The cross-plane door may open, but behind the door there must be a ledger.</p><p>Causal self-discipline absence also makes the transmigrator forever young. He need not be responsible for his own disturbance, so he can stay naive. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s supervision wants the transmigrator to also grow old — responsible for every cross-plane operation he makes; this is a mature cross-plane civilization.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: disturbance uncorrected; external variable no feedback loop</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: free-take time-difference dividend; no settlement of cross-plane bill</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo was native, no such problem; Ji Ning and Tang San both owe a karmic bill</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: native Myriad Ranks become soil for transmigrator arbitrage</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: cross-plane unregulated; the more crossing, the messier causality</li></ul><p>Causal self-discipline absence also traps the transmigrator in a paradox: the more successful he is, the larger the disturbance, the heavier the future karmic debt. The more Ji Ning reaches the peak in Manghuang, the deeper his change on Manghuang&#39;s causality — this change should have been recorded, evaluated, corrected, yet is written off. What Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s causal supervision wants to do is precisely not let the transmigrator&#39;s success become a check that never cashes. Cross-plane prosperity cannot be built on debt default.</p><p>The cross-plane bill must be repaid sooner or later. Heng Yuan Zhou only establishes this ledger in advance, not letting the transmigrator default until the last moment. The door may open; the ledger must be kept.</p><p>The cross-plane door opens beautifully, premise is the ledger kept clearly.</p><p>Causal self-discipline is the cross-plane civilization&#39;s coming-of-age rite.</p><p>This ledger, cross-plane civilizations sooner or later must learn to keep.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Transmigration is not the original sin; airdropping without filing is. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s causal self-discipline is plain: you may bring knowledge, but may not take away causality; you may observe, may not freely rewrite. Ji Ning enjoyed the dividend of transmigration, yet never learned to knock first — this bill, Manghuang&#39;s world no one calculates for him.</p><p>In the final analysis, Manghuang Ji · causal self-discipline absence · transmigrators and causal disturbance described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./428_模块2-莽荒纪-文明权重分析-纪宁个人权重碾压文明共识.html">Entry 428 · Civilizational-Weight Analysis</a> · <a href="./412_模块2-莽荒纪-纪宁vs唐三-莽荒与斗罗的穿越者对比.html">Entry 412 · Ji Ning vs. Tang San</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/83-先观测后有限干涉准则.html">83-Observe-First-Then-Limited-Interference Principle</a></li></ul>',33)])])}const m=i(s,[["render",o]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
